# Checkpoints v1.1 Implementation Plan

> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.

**Goal:** Store v1 checkpoint metadata at the custom ref `refs/entire/checkpoints/v1` (outside `refs/heads/`) when `strategy_options.checkpoints_version` is set to `1.1` in `.entire/settings.json`, while preserving existing v1 history through a one-shot ref initialization on first access.

**Architecture:** A single resolver function (`checkpoint.MetadataRef`) returns the active metadata ref based on settings. All read and write sites that previously hardcoded the branch ref now go through the resolver. A separate `checkpoint.PreserveV1History` is invoked from both write paths (via `EnsureMetadataBranch`) and read entry points to initialize the custom ref at the legacy branch's tip on first access. The push hook is generalized to take full ref names so the existing rebase-on-non-FF recovery works at the custom-ref namespace.

**Tech Stack:** Go 1.26.x, go-git v6 (`github.com/go-git/go-git/v6`), cobra, mise.

**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-05-20-checkpoints-v1.1-design.md`

